22
00:00:29,293 --> 00:00:30,987
Its formulas stay in the cells,

23
00:00:30,997 --> 00:00:31,626
like shown work:

24
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:32,479
you can check how

25
00:00:32,489 --> 00:00:34,193
each number was calculated.

26
00:00:34,443 --> 00:00:35,906
If our total skipped a quarter,

27
00:00:35,916 --> 00:00:37,021
its formula shows it!

28
00:00:37,271 --> 00:00:40,187
Claude's edits are outlined as they land;

29
00:00:40,197 --> 00:00:43,197
a card can undo just those, briefly.

30
00:00:43,447 --> 00:00:44,927
So, what we learned:

31
00:00:44,937 --> 00:00:47,085
our three pasted totals showed no work;

32
00:00:47,095 --> 00:00:48,524
in the paid-plan beta,

33
00:00:48,534 --> 00:00:50,453
they can be formulas you check.

34
00:00:50,703 --> 00:00:51,930
